# Call Coaching Software: The 5 Best Tools for Sales Teams in 2026, Compared

By [Samarth Wagh](https://lynkk.ai/blog/authors/samarth-wagh) · 4 November 2026 · Competitor facts checked against each vendor's public site in October 2026

> **Quick answer:** The best call coaching software for large teams is Gong or Clari Copilot, both quote-only, with Gong seats reported at about **$1,200 to $2,400 a year**. Mid-size teams get coaching from Avoma (a **$29** add-on) or Fathom's Business plan scorecards. Small teams that coach from recordings can use Lynkk at **$15** a month, which records and searches calls but doesn't score them.

Call coaching software is a tool that records sales calls, analyses them, and shows managers what to coach, such as talk time, questions asked, or how objections were handled. The category overlaps with conversation intelligence, but the job is narrower: help a manager make one rep better, one call at a time.

> **Disclosure:** This guide is published by Lynkk. Lynkk is a meeting recorder, not a coaching suite, and we say where it falls short below. Competitor facts come from each vendor's public pages, checked in October 2026.

## Our quick picks

| Tool | Best for | Coaching features | Price |
|---|---|---|---|
| Gong | Large teams with RevOps | Call analysis, coaching, deal intelligence, forecasting | Quote only; about $1,200 to $2,400 a seat a year reported |
| Clari Copilot | Teams already on Clari or Salesloft | Coaching scorecards, live battlecards, deal risk | Quote only; about $120 to $160 a user a month reported |
| Avoma | Mid-market revenue teams | Coaching and scorecards as an add-on | $19 a seat a month yearly, plus $29 for coaching |
| Fathom | Teams that want scorecards cheaply | AI scorecards and coaching metrics on Business | Business $34 a user a month, $25 yearly |
| Lynkk | Small teams coaching from recordings | Searchable calls, no scoring | Free plan; Pro $15 a month |

## What is call coaching software?

These tools record and transcribe sales calls, then highlight the moments a manager should review, such as long monologues, missed questions or a competitor mention. Most tools add scorecards, so a manager can rate calls against the same 5 to 10 criteria every time.

It matters because sales coaching is the lever most teams under-use. A 2020 Training Industry article cites CSO Insights research that coaching "had the greatest impact on win rates and quota attainment", and Aberdeen research showing dynamic coaching lifted win rates 19.0% above the study average, per [Training Industry](https://trainingindustry.com/magazine/mar-apr-2020/driving-sales-training-results-through-manager-coaching-cptm/).

## What is the best call coaching software?

The best sales call coaching software depends on team size and budget. Gong suits large teams, Clari Copilot suits Clari or Salesloft shops, Avoma and Fathom suit mid-size teams, and Lynkk suits small teams that coach from recordings. Here's what each does well, and where it doesn't fit.

### 1. Gong: best for large sales teams with RevOps

Gong is the best-known revenue intelligence platform, and its call analysis, deal intelligence and forecasting are hard to match on a large team. It publishes no prices and has no free plan. Buyer reports put seats at about $1,200 to $2,400 a year, plus a platform fee, on contracts of 1 to 3 years, per our [Lynkk vs Gong comparison](https://lynkk.ai/compare/gong).

- **Pick it if:** you have a RevOps team to run it and want coaching tied to forecasting.
- **Skip it if:** you want to start this week, or need a published price.

### 2. Clari Copilot: best for teams already on Clari or Salesloft

Clari Copilot is the conversation intelligence product Clari built from Wingman, which it bought in 2022. It records calls, runs coaching scorecards, flags deal risk, and shows battlecards live when a competitor comes up. Clari and Salesloft merged in December 2025, and buyer reports put standalone Copilot at about $120 to $160 a user a month on a 12-month minimum, per our [Clari Copilot comparison](https://lynkk.ai/compare/clari-copilot).

- **Pick it if:** you already run Clari or Salesloft and want live battlecards.
- **Skip it if:** you don't want a 12-month contract.

### 3. Avoma: best for mid-market revenue teams

Avoma combines meeting notes, conversation intelligence, CRM updates, scheduling and coaching. Its Startup plan is $19 a seat a month billed yearly, and coaching and forecasting are $29 add-ons on top ($35 billed monthly), per [Avoma's pricing page](https://www.avoma.com/pricing) and our [Lynkk vs Avoma comparison](https://lynkk.ai/compare/avoma). It offers a 14-day trial rather than a free plan.

- **Pick it if:** you want coaching, scorecards and scheduling in one tool.
- **Skip it if:** you need a free plan that keeps recording after the trial.

### 4. Fathom: best for scorecards on a budget

Fathom is a meeting recorder with a free-forever plan, and its paid plans lean toward sales teams. AI scorecards and coaching metrics sit on the Business plan, at $34 a user a month or $25 billed yearly, with a 2-user minimum, per [Fathom's pricing page](https://fathom.ai/pricing). Premium is $20 and Team is $19 a user a month, and our [Lynkk vs Fathom comparison](https://lynkk.ai/compare/fathom) covers the rest.

- **Pick it if:** you want call scorecards without an enterprise contract.
- **Skip it if:** many of your sales meetings happen in a room, not on a call.

### 5. Lynkk: best for small teams that coach from recordings

Lynkk records Zoom, Google Meet and Teams calls, or meetings in a room from the Mac app, and turns each one into a transcript, summary and action items. It doesn't score calls or run coaching workflows. On Pro, [Ask Lynkk](https://lynkk.ai/features/ask-your-meetings) answers questions like "how did we handle pricing pushback last month?" across every note, with the minute behind each answer.

- **Pick it if:** you coach by listening to real calls and want them searchable for $15 a month.
- **Skip it if:** you need scorecards, CRM sync or forecasting.

## How does AI call coaching software work?

AI coaching tools work in 4 steps: record the call, transcribe it, analyse the transcript against coaching criteria, and surface the moments worth reviewing. The analysis is what separates coaching tools from plain recorders.

1. **Record:** a bot joins the call, or a desktop app captures it.
2. **Transcribe:** speech-to-text labels who said what.
3. **Analyse:** the AI measures talk time, questions, monologues and topics like pricing or competitors.
4. **Surface:** managers get flagged moments, scorecards or a coaching queue.

The metrics come from research on real calls. Gong's study of [519,000 discovery calls](https://www.gong.io/blog/deal-closing-discovery-call/) linked 11 to 14 questions to the best results, which is exactly the kind of benchmark these tools score against.

## What is live sales call coaching?

Live sales call coaching means getting prompts during the call, such as a battlecard when a competitor is named or a suggested answer to an objection. Clari Copilot shows battlecards in the moment, and most other tools coach after the call instead.

Lynkk's [Spotter](https://lynkk.ai/features/spotter) is a live assistant for the Mac with a Sales mode for objections and pricing questions, built from your own notes. It's in development, with early access open, and it stays visible in screen shares. For the techniques it supports, see our guide to [objection handling](https://lynkk.ai/blog/objection-handling).

## What is the difference between call coaching and call monitoring software?

Call monitoring software lets a manager listen to calls, often live, for quality and compliance. Coaching tools go a step further: they analyse calls, score them and build a plan to improve each rep.

| | Call monitoring software | Call coaching tools |
|---|---|---|
| Main job | Quality and compliance checks | Improving rep skills |
| Typical user | Contact-centre supervisor | Sales manager or enablement lead |
| Output | Listen-in, whisper, barge, call logs | Scorecards, flagged moments, coaching plans |

## How much does call coaching software cost?

Prices range from free to about $160 a user a month among the tools here. Enterprise platforms like Gong and Clari Copilot are quote-only, with buyer reports of $1,200 to $2,400 a seat a year for Gong and $120 to $160 a user a month for Copilot.

Mid-market tools publish prices: Avoma starts at $19 a seat a month yearly plus a $29 coaching add-on, and Fathom's Business plan, which includes scorecards, is $34 a user a month. Lynkk Pro is $15 a month, or $117 a year, per its [pricing page](https://lynkk.ai/pricing). Budget for the contract length too, because 1 to 3 year terms change the real cost.

## What is the best call center coaching software?

The best call center coaching software usually sits inside or alongside your contact-centre platform. It has to handle phone queues, live listen-in and quality scoring at high volume. Sales-focused tools like the five above are built for video calls and deals, not ticket queues.

If you run a contact centre, ask any vendor for 3 things: live whisper or listen-in for supervisors, automated quality scoring on every call, and integration with your telephony system.

## How do you run a sales call coaching session?

Run a sales call coaching session in 30 minutes. Pick one recorded call, play 2 or 3 short moments, agree one thing to change, and check it on the next call. One skill per session beats a long list of fixes.

Here's a simple sales call coaching template:

| Step | Minutes | What happens |
|---|---|---|
| Pick | Before | Manager chooses one call and 2 or 3 moments |
| Self-review | 5 | Rep says what went well and what they'd change |
| Listen | 10 | Play each moment together, then pause and discuss |
| Agree | 10 | Pick one skill to practise, with a role-play |
| Follow up | 5 | Book a check on the next 2 calls |

The [conversation intelligence guide](https://lynkk.ai/blog/sales-conversation-intelligence) covers how to pick which calls to review first.

## How do you choose call coaching software?

Match the tool to how your managers actually coach, then check price, contract and recording options. Of all the call coaching tools on a shortlist, the one nobody opens is the most expensive.

- **Coaching style:** do managers want scorecards, or just searchable recordings?
- **Live vs after:** do reps need prompts during the call, or reviews after it?
- **Recording:** does it need a bot in the call, or can it record without one?
- **Price and term:** is the price published, and how long is the contract?
- **Team size:** enterprise platforms pay off with RevOps support; small teams need simpler tools.

## FAQ

### Does call coaching improve win rates?

Research suggests it does. Aberdeen research, cited by Training Industry in 2020, found dynamic coaching lifted win rates 19.0% and quota attainment 21.3% above the study average. The studies are a few years old, so treat the exact figures as directional, but the finding that regular, specific coaching helps has been consistent.

### Is there free call coaching software?

Few coaching tools are fully free. Fathom has a free-forever plan for recording, with scorecards on its Business plan, and Lynkk's free plan records unlimited meetings with the first 5 hours of AI notes included. Gong and Clari Copilot have no free plan, and Avoma offers a 14-day trial instead.

### Can you coach sales reps from Zoom recordings?

Yes. Any recorded Zoom, Google Meet or Teams call can be used for coaching. Pick two or three short moments, listen with the rep, and agree on one change. An AI note taker makes this faster, because you can search transcripts for objections or pricing instead of scrubbing through hours of video.

### What is a call coaching form?

A call coaching form is a one-page scorecard a manager fills in while reviewing a call. It usually covers the opening, discovery questions, objection handling, next steps and talk time, each with a score and a note. Keep it to 5 to 10 criteria, so reviews stay fast and consistent across reps.

### How often should you coach sales reps?

Most sales teams coach weekly, with one short session per rep built around a recent call. Consistency matters more than length: 30 minutes every week beats a long review once a quarter. New reps often need two sessions a week for their first month, then move to the weekly rhythm.

### Does Gong have a free plan?

No. Gong publishes no prices and has no free plan or self-serve checkout. Buying it means a sales cycle and usually a contract of one to three years. Buyer reports put seats at about $1,200 to $2,400 a year, plus a platform fee, based on Lynkk's October 2026 comparison.

## Conclusion

The right tool is the one your managers will open every week. Large teams with RevOps get the most from Gong or Clari Copilot, mid-size teams from Avoma or Fathom, and small teams can coach well from searchable recordings in Lynkk. For the questions worth coaching on, start with our [discovery call questions](https://lynkk.ai/blog/discovery-call-questions).

**Try Lynkk.** It records your sales calls and makes every moment searchable for coaching. [Start for free](https://lynkk.ai/).

